# cc-admins-admin-session - the scoped sudo grant for the admin helper.
# [PLANNED - install ONLY on the ADMIN AMI, never on an engineer VDI or a
# shared on-prem host without review. See docs/LOCAL-VS-AWS.md.]
#
# Install to /etc/sudoers.d/cc-admins-admin-session, root:root 0440, and validate
# with `visudo -cf` BEFORE it takes effect - a syntax error here can lock out sudo.
#
# WHAT THIS GRANTS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
# One command: members of the LDAP group cc-admins may run the hardened, logged
# wrapper /usr/local/sbin/cc-admin-session.sh as root, with no password prompt.
# It is an ALLOWLIST ENTRY, not general root - the wrapper runs the agent as the
# invoker under the loose admin policy and stamps admin.log.
#
# HARD PRECONDITION: cc-admin-session.sh must enforce its target-user policy
# (RUN_AS == invoker, never uid 0). Without it, `... -u root` turns this one-line
# grant back into unrestricted root. Do not deploy this rule against a wrapper
# that lacks it. Verify: the wrapper's header carries the "TARGET-USER POLICY"
# block.
#
# NOPASSWD is deliberate: the engineer has no other sudo on the box, so there is
# no blanket grant sitting next to this that a password would need to guard, and
# a non-interactive admin task would otherwise hang on a prompt. If a password
# step is ever wanted, change NOPASSWD: to PASSWD: - it authenticates the
# invoker's own account via sssd/LDAP.
#
# NOTE docs/ADMIN-SESSION.md states the position for a shared host, where the
# invoker may hold other sudo rights. Both positions are reconciled in
# docs/LOCAL-VS-AWS.md §8.4; do not change one alone.
#
# NOSETENV is load-bearing, not decoration. cc-admin-session.sh's config loader
# honours $CC_CONFIG_LIB FIRST in its search order and sources it as root
# without validation. That is safe only while sudo's env_reset default strips
# the variable; a site that adds `Defaults setenv` or a matching env_keep would
# make `sudo CC_CONFIG_LIB=/tmp/evil.sh cc-admin-session.sh` arbitrary code as
# root - full root through a different door than -u root, defeating the whole
# point of a one-command allowlist. NOSETENV refuses the per-command override
# regardless of the site default.
%cc-admins ALL=(root) NOPASSWD:NOSETENV: /usr/local/sbin/cc-admin-session.sh
